# Theme updates

## Source versions

- New theme drops go in `themes/` (e.g. `themes/trafigura-vX/`).
- When asked to update from a version there, merge/adapt into the live theme root (not leave the site running from `themes/`).
- Preserve local customizations (listed below + SEO folder + this rules folder) unless the user says otherwise.

## After every theme sync — re-apply checklist

Run through these; Udesly/Webflow exports often wipe them.

### 1. News & partner stories order (required)

In `template-parts/query/`:

- All `news-*.php` queries: `"order" => "DESC"`
- All `partner-stories-*.php` queries: `"order" => "DESC"`

Do **not** leave Webflow/Udesly defaults of `"order" => "ASC"`.

```php
// ❌ BAD — oldest first
"order" => "ASC",

// ✅ GOOD — newest first
"order" => "DESC",
```

### 2. Content Hub H1 casing

- File: `template-parts/content/page-content-hub.php`
- H1 must be **`Content Hub`** (not lowercase `content hub` from Udesly `_u()`).
- Prefer hardcoded text over `_u('tn17498f32','text')` so DB/editor overrides cannot regress it.
- Also keep `_data/frontend-editor/page-content-hub.json` key `tn17498f32` = `Content Hub`.

### 3. Homepage performance (hero video + GTM)

**Poster assets (must exist):**

- `assets/images/home-hero-poster.jpg` (video `poster` / fallback)
- `assets/images/home-hero-poster-960.webp` (LCP `<img src>` — ~26 KiB)
- Optional: `home-hero-poster-960.jpg`, `home-hero-poster-1280.webp`

**`template-parts/content/front-page.php` — home hero:**

- Show local poster `<img class="hero-poster no-lazy">` with `src` = `home-hero-poster-960.webp`, `fetchpriority="high"`, `loading="eager"`, `data-no-lazy="1"`, width/height set (W3TC must not lazy-load it).
- Do **not** put `<source src="...">` in the HTML (avoids downloading ~6.7MB Webflow video on mobile).
- Video wrap starts with `hidden`; element keeps `data-mp4` / `data-webm` from `_u('i-5fdbe129')` / `_u('i64642473')`.
- Inline script loads sources **only** when `min-width: 992px` and not `prefers-reduced-motion`, after `window.load` + ~3s delay; reveal with `wrap.hidden = false` after `loadeddata`.
- Mobile / reduced-motion: poster only.
- Homepage uses footer partial `footer/front-page` (wired in `front-page.php`).
- Homepage H1 must **not** use `animation="loading"` (GSAP starts those at opacity 0 and delays LCP).
- Do **not** defer GSAP/Swiper/`script.js` until after load — that caused blank filmstrip / LCP regression.

**`template-parts/head/front-page.php`:**

- Preload **WebP** poster only (not both WebP + JPEG):  
  `<link rel="preload" as="image" href=".../home-hero-poster-960.webp" type="image/webp" fetchpriority="high">`
- Preload Euclid medium woff2 (`crossorigin`).
- Small CSS for `.hero-poster` / `.hero-video-wrap` / `[hidden]`; hide video wrap on `max-width: 991px`.

**Rem root (all pages — CLS/LCP):**

- `header.php` must load `template-parts/head/partials/rem-root.php` **before** other head CSS.
- Contains Webflow `html { font-size: calc(100vw/…) }` breakpoints (same as body embeds).
- Leaving rem scaling only in body embeds causes a late layout snap (CLS).
- Do **not** add `scrollbar-gutter: stable` or desktop navbar `min-width` reserves — user wants content to shift when nav opens; no permanent empty left column.

**Navbar width (desktop):**

- Default `.navbar { width: 0 }` — menu panel is `position: absolute` (`.navbar--menu` stays `width: 272rem`).
- At `min-width: 1752px` (inlined `code/style.css` rules in staging): `.navbar { width: 272rem !important }` and menu always visible.
- IX2 opens the nav and expands width so content shifts — do **not** force `min-width: 272rem` on closed nav.

**GTM (all templates):**

- Shared partial: `template-parts/head/partials/gtm-deferred.php`
- Keep GTM (analytics); **gtag/GA loads from the GTM container** — do not add a separate gtag snippet.
- Load on first interaction **or** idle (timeout ~6s) — do **not** restore the blocking GTM snippet.

### 3b. Fonts (all self-hosted — no Google Fonts)

- Prefer `assets/fonts/euclid-circular-b-*.woff2` in CSS `@font-face` (weights **400 / 500 / 600** only; map light→400, bold→600 if export brings 300/700).
- **`font-display: optional`** on Euclid **and** Bebas (all `@font-face` blocks, including the duplicate faces at the end of staging). This cuts desktop CLS from late font swap on `#smooth-content` hero text. Keep homepage **preload** of Euclid medium so it usually wins the optional race.
- Bebas Neue files: `assets/fonts/bebas-neue-regular.woff2`, `bebas-neue-regular-latin-ext.woff2`, `bebas-neue-regular.ttf`.
- `bebas-font.php` must **not** load `fonts.googleapis.com` / `fonts.gstatic.com` — keep only the Webflow `w-mod-js` / touch class bootstrap.
- Keep `elementor/frontend/print_google_fonts` → false (no Elementor Roboto from Google).
- Enqueue **one** CSS file: `assets/css/trafigura-bundle.css` (= normalize + components + staging, minified for ship). Rebuild after editing sources:

```bash
cat assets/css/normalize.css assets/css/components.css assets/css/trafigura-staging.css > assets/css/trafigura-bundle.css
# then minify for production (or ship unminified while debugging)
```

- Bump `ver=` on `wp_enqueue_style('trafigura-bundle', …)` in all `template-parts/head/*.php` after CSS changes (cache bust / W3TC).

### 3c. Listing images (card src + OceanImageBank)

**`functions.php` helpers:**

- `trafigura_card_image( $sizes )` — prefers `medium_large` + `sizes`; used by news/partner listing query templates
- `trafigura_optimized_image_override( $thumb_id )` — serves theme-compressed copies from `assets/images/optimized/` for known heavy uploads (e.g. `OceanImageBank_AriphRasheed_07`)

**Re-wire after sync:** any `news-*.php` / `partner-stories-*.php` card `<img>` that still uses raw `udesly_get_image()->src` should use `trafigura_card_image()` instead.

### 3d. Render-blocking cleanup (keep in `functions.php` + `footer.php`)

- `trafigura_dequeue_unused_assets()` — dequeues block-library, Elementor Roboto fonts, Elementor frontend/kit CSS when no real Elementor content (`trafigura_page_needs_elementor_css()`), honeypot/udesly common CSS
- `elementor/frontend/print_google_fonts` → false
- `trafigura_jquery_in_footer()` marks jQuery footer-group; **`footer.php` calls `wp_print_scripts( 'jquery' )` immediately before** theme/GSAP/Swiper/`code/` scripts
- Host former Netlify extras from theme `code/` — do **not** restore `https://trafigura-code.netlify.app/...` URLs
- Self-host under `assets/js/vendor/`: `gsap.min.js`, `ScrollTrigger.min.js`, `CustomEase.min.js`, `swiper-bundle.min.js` (v11), `swiper10-bundle.min.js` + `.css` (tales), `split-type.min.js` — do **not** restore cdnjs / jsDelivr / unpkg
- Helpers: `trafigura_code_uri( $path )`, `trafigura_vendor_uri( $path )`
- `trafigura_dequeue_unused_scripts()` — dequeue honeypot/`wpa.js` by handle **and** src; dequeue Udesly frontend-editor chunks for **public** visitors only (keep for logged-in / preview); **keep jquery-migrate**
- `code/style.css` is **inlined** into `trafigura-staging.css` (marker comment) — do not link Netlify/`code/style.css` separately in heads
- **Never** set `.main-wrapper { opacity: 0 }` waiting for GSAP — blanks filmstrip / destroys mobile FCP
- `code/script.js`: guard Swiper inits with `if (typeof Swiper !== "undefined")` so homepage/pages without Swiper do not throw; do not fade entire `.main-wrapper` on load

**Footer script pattern (typical page):** jQuery → `trafigura-staging.js` → vendor GSAP trio → (Swiper if needed) → `code/script.js` (+ page JS). Homepage: `template-parts/footer/front-page.php` includes Swiper (partner slider uses `.swiper.is--slider-resources`). Tales: Swiper 10 CSS in head, JS in footer; SplitType from local vendor.

### 3e. Partner story singles — areas tag (SEO links, visually hidden)

In `template-parts/content/single-partner-stories.php`:

- Keep place + state tags visible.
- Areas-of-work tag stays in HTML (pillar links via `trafigura_link_areas_of_work_text()`) but is hidden:

```php
<div class="tag--item is--areas-of-work" hidden>
  <div class=""><?php echo trafigura_link_areas_of_work_text( $partner_areas ); ?></div>
</div>
```

- CSS: `.tag--item.is--areas-of-work[hidden] { display: none !important; }` (needed because `.tag--item { display: flex }` would override the HTML `hidden` attribute).

### 4. Internal linking helpers + templates

**`functions.php` — keep these helpers:**

- `trafigura_area_of_work_url( $slug )`
- `trafigura_link_areas_of_work_text( $text )` — turns PlainText area labels into pillar links
- `trafigura_card_image( $sizes )` / `trafigura_optimized_image_override( $thumb_id )`
- `trafigura_code_uri( $path )` / `trafigura_vendor_uri( $path )`

